  "definition": "An IoT sensor is a networked device that measures physical or environmental conditions \u2014 such as temperature, humidity, location, vibration or light \u2014 and transmits the resulting data over a communications network to back-end systems for monitoring and analysis. By embedding sensing and connectivity into assets and environments, IoT sensors provide continuous, real-time visibility that supports automation and data-driven decisions. In supply chains they are central to cold-chain monitoring, asset tracking and condition-based maintenance.",
